/T (What is an inherited genetic disorder?)
/E (What is an inherited genetic disorder?)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
85 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 66 0 R
/E (Our bodies are built using instructions stored in our DNA. You can think of DNA like a very large instruction book. Inside it are smaller sections called genes. These genes help tell the body how to grow, develop, and work. We usually get one copy of each gene from our mother and one copy from our father. Sometimes, a gene contains a change that affects how the body works. If this change causes a health condition and can be passed from parent to child, it may cause an inherited genetic disorder.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
86 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 66 0 R
/E (Examples include:)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
