<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 68 0 R
/E (Some genetic conditions are called recessive disorders. For many recessive disorders, a person needs to inherit a changed copy of the same gene from both parents to develop the condition. A person who has only one changed copy is usually called a carrier. Carriers are often completely healthy.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [2]
>>
