111 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 70 0 R
/E (This can happen when both parents are healthy carriers. Neither parent has the disorder because each still has one working copy of the gene. However, if their child receives the changed copy from both parents, the child may develop the condition. This is common in recessive genetic disorders. It is one reason family history alone cannot always tell us whether someone is a carrier.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
