/Pg 20 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
129 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 74 0 R
/E (Not necessarily. For many genetic disorders, each pregnancy has its own chance. For example, if both parents are carriers of the same recessive disorder, the chance of an affected child is usually 25% in every pregnancy. Having one affected child does not make the next child automatically affected. Having one healthy child also does not remove the risk for the next pregnancy.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
